====================================================================================================
A. Identities, checked for every integer -20000 <= n <= 20000
====================================================================================================
  True   NOT(3n+1) = 3 NOT(n) + 1            (3x+1 commutes with NOT)
  True   NOT(NOT(m)/2) = (m-1)/2, m odd       (halving does NOT commute)
  True   NOT o T o NOT = TN: m -> 3m/2 (m even), (m-1)/2 (m odd)
  True   TN(m) = Tminus(m+1) - 1              (TN is 3x-1 shifted by one)
  True   -T(-y) = Tminus(y)                   (negation: 3x+1 on Z_<0 = 3x-1 on Z_>0)
  True   T_NOT(n) = T_n                       (triangular number is NOT-invariant)
  True   T_(3n+1) = 9 T_n + 1                 (the odd step descends to t -> 9t+1)
  True   u(3n+1) = 3 u(n),  u = 2n+1
  True   u(n/2) = v(n) = n+1 for n even
  True   v(T(n)) = 3v/2 (v even), (v+1)/2 (v odd),  v = n+1
  True   T(NOT(e)) = NOT(3e/2) for e even     (mirror branch of an even point)
  halving has no image in the t = T_n coordinate: T_n = T_NOT(n), but only one of n, NOT(n) is even.
  The two branches at the even representative e of the pair {e, NOT(e)} are  e -> e/2  (3x+1 side)
  and  e -> 3e/2  (mirror side): the quotient by NOT is a 2-valued correspondence, not a map.

